Settings
--------
Create a text file <Choices$Write>.SSHd.Options with one setting per line
(it survives package upgrades, which replace !Run):
  port 22                 TCP port to listen on
  root <Boot$Dir>.^       directory SFTP clients start in
  bind 0.0.0.0            address to listen on (all interfaces)
  verbose 0               1 for more log lines, 2 for SSH protocol detail
  log on                  off to stop writing <Choices$Write>.SSHd.log
Lines starting with # are comments.  The log file keeps the same lines as
the log window and is started afresh when it grows past 256 KB; it is
where to look after a crash.

Command line options override the file (run sshd by hand in a TaskWindow
with -t for text mode): -p port, -d config-dir, -r sftp-dir, -b address,
-t, -v.

If the server cannot start (no CryptRandom module, port in use), the icon
stays on the bar, the log window opens with the reason, and Quit removes
it; nothing blocks a boot sequence that runs !SSHd.

After upgrading the package, Quit the running !SSHd and run the new one;
the Info window shows which version is running.
